contentText:
It&#8217;s not all bad news for Boosie Badazz .

The Louisiana rapper reunited with a childhood friend while he visited Detroit to perform at the Aretha Franklin Amphitheatre for his national tour &#8220; Boosie Badazz & Friends: Blues on the River V ,&#8221; as he finds himself in the middle of various legal battles that involve a lawsuit over an alleged assault by hookah at a nightclub and a legal action he recently filed after a failed presidential pardon effort.

Last month, Boosie posted a Reel on Instagram asking his followers to give him some feedback on a heartfelt email he was thinking of sending to his long lost childhood best friend, Derrick, who moved from Baton Rouge, Louisiana to Michigan when they were kids. &#8220;Aye, I think I found my long lost friend,&#8221; he said to the camera. &#8220;I got an email on &#8217;em, so I&#8217;m finna email him. Y&#8217;all tell me how this email sounds.&#8221; He then began reading the message where he talked about all the good times they had growing up while attending Wildwood Elementary and referred to his old friend as his &#8220;bestie&#8221; before leaving his number for him to reach out.

When he was done reading the email, someone in the background could be heard saying, &#8220;That was so sweet and sentimental.&#8221;

However, the comments on the post took a predictably different tone. Some joked around about how serious the email sounded with one of those people being Derrick himself who left a comment with laughing emojis telling his buddy to get in touch. &#8220;You wrote that s—t like I’m on my death bed,&#8221; he joked. &#8220;I’m crying laughing….who you emailing!?? I’m waiting on the contact. Wow this is crazy…Derrick Jackson Jr on Facebook.&#8221;

The two old friends did indeed get in touch and the Baton Rouge rapper posted separate vids of him pulling up on his childhood bestie&#8217;s house where the two gave each other a big hug and another of the two of them being kids again at Slick City Action Park where they raced down slides together with one of the captions reading , &#8220;Back like we ain&#8217;t never separated! We compete at everything.&#8221;

DetroitRapDaily then caught up with Derrick where he shared the reply he would&#8217;ve sent back had he gotten the email and admitted that people never believed him whenever he would tell them he knew Boosie when they were kids. &#8220;Bro, it&#8217;s been 30 years since I left Baton Rouge to move back to Michigan,&#8221; he began. &#8220;I always truly believed we would cross paths again in the same exact way. Your videos explaining your flashback to our childhood friendship brought many memories that I share with my friends and my family here in my hometown. Now many never truly believed I really knew the real Boosie Badazz, now I&#8217;m looking forward to renewing our friendship like it never stopped, bro. Sincerely, Derrick Jackson.&#8221;
